  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data visualization and leveraging AI. The project was introduced by Alex with Sarah Tan as the lead, starting with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial phase budget of $500,000. Emily called for R&D proposals by July 20th to enhance data visualization tools. Initial findings reported by Tom suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase from AI algorithms, to be discussed on August 5th. Following the design phase, Omar Jensen leads the development phase. A major milestone was reached ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, with UI enhancements planned for October. The project is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Additionally, the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000, and a $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
